%requires qore >= 2.0
%modern

%requires(reexport) QoreLlmTypes
%requires(reexport) RestClientIo

%requires json

module GeminiBodyShape {
    version = "1.0.0";
    desc = "Shared Gemini generateContent wire format: request/response shapers "
        "plus the common AbstractGeminiModelProvider base — shared between the "
        "native GeminiRestClient provider and the Vertex AI Gemini-on-Vertex "
        "pathway so the two cannot drift on tool/option/response handling";
    author = "Qore Technologies, s.r.o.";
    url = "https://qore.org";
    license = "MIT";
}

/** @mainpage GeminiBodyShape Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section geminibodyshapeintro Introduction to the GeminiBodyShape Module

    The %GeminiBodyShape module exposes the pure-static helpers that
    translate between the generic @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage /
    @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse types and the Google Gemini
    \c generateContent wire format.  The native provider in
    @ref geminirestclientintro "GeminiRestClient"
    uses these helpers; the Vertex AI Gemini-on-Vertex pathway also depends
    on them so the two providers stay in lock-step as Gemini evolves.

    All functions are pure-static — no I/O, no state — so callers can mix
    and match them as needed.  @ref AbstractGeminiModelProvider implements
    chat, completion, and \c streamGenerateContent SSE streaming on top of
    them; the transport and authentication remain in the host provider.

    @par Function inventory

    Request-side:
    - @ref shapeChatBody() — full request-body builder (counterpart to the
      legacy private \c buildGeminiBody method)
    - @ref shapeChatRequest() — the request body plus the tool arguments that it
      declares as JSON strings
    - @ref shapeContentParts() — multimodal parts from a
      @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage
    - @ref sanitizeSchema() — strip JSON Schema keywords Gemini rejects and
      resolve references and alternatives
    - @ref shapeToolParameters() — the Gemini form of a tool's parameter schema
      (see @ref geminibodyshapetoolschemas)
    - @ref openAiToolChoiceToGeminiConfig() — adapt OpenAI \c tool_choice
      to Gemini \c toolConfig
    - @ref normalizeGenerationConfig() — model-specific generation controls, applied after body overrides
    - @ref applyCachedContent() — make a request use a cached content resource
      (explicit prompt caching)
    - @ref shapeCachedContentBody() / @ref shapeCacheExpiration() — the bodies
      of \c cachedContents create and update requests

    Response-side:
    - @ref parseChatResponse() — Gemini response → @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse
    - @ref parseToolResponse() — adapt OpenAI tool-result strings for
      Gemini \c functionResponse.response
    - @ref decodeToolArguments() / @ref decodeResponseToolArguments() — return
      tool-call arguments with the types of the original tool schema
      (@ref encodeToolArguments() is the inverse)
    - @ref extractText() — concatenate text parts in a Gemini response
    - @ref normalizeUsage() — Gemini \c usageMetadata → OpenAI-style counters
    - @ref mapFinishReason() / @ref finishReasonToOpenAi() — finish-reason
      vocabulary normalization
    - @ref providerDiagnostics() — surface Gemini-specific diagnostics

    Model-name utilities:
    - @ref modelResource() — \c "models/<name>" canonicalization
    - @ref bareModelName() — strip \c "models/" prefix

    @section geminibodyshapegeneration Generation parameters

    Gemini and Vertex AI select generation parameters using the effective model for each request, including
    per-call model overrides. For Gemini 3.x, \c temperature, \c topP and \c topK are omitted even when
    supplied in \c body_options. Use \c reasoning_effort to set \c generationConfig.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel:
    \c minimal, \c low, \c medium or \c high. The provider-neutral \c xhigh and \c max values map to \c HIGH.
    Supported levels depend on the model; for example Gemini 3.1 Pro does not support \c minimal.
    An explicit native thinking level in \c body_options takes precedence.

    Numeric \c reasoning_token_budget values (including zero and -1) are omitted on Gemini 3.x, since a token
    budget has no exact thinking-level equivalent. Without an explicit level, the model default applies.
    Gemini 3.x cannot fully disable thinking; \c disable_reasoning is therefore not mapped to a level.
    Older models, including Gemini 2.5, retain sampling parameters and numeric thinking budgets. Generic
    \c reasoning_effort is ignored for these models; Gemini 2.5's generateContent API does not accept thinking levels.

    @par Example
    An invoice classifier using either the Gemini or Vertex LLM provider can limit reasoning depth per request:
    @code{.py}
provider.complete("Classify invoices by department", invoice_text, NOTHING,
    <QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions>{"model": "gemini-3.1-pro-preview", "reasoning_effort": "low"});
    @endcode

    Direct data-provider requests use \c generationConfig.thinkingConfig.thinkingLevel; Gemini's simple-chat
    action accepts \c thinkingConfig directly. All generation actions normalize their final request before
    sending it, including streaming. Raw generic REST calls remain caller-controlled.

    See https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/generate-content/thinking and
    https://docs.cloud.google.com/gemini-enterprise-agent-platform/models/migrate for Google's model guidance.

    @section geminibodyshapetoolschemas Tool parameter schemas

    Gemini fills a function call's arguments with a constrained decoder that follows the declared parameter schema:
    it can only produce the members that the schema declares, so an object declared without its members is always
    sent as \c {}.  The decoder compiles the function declarations of a request into one state machine, and Google
    states that very large or deeply nested schemas may be rejected, which Gemini reports as
    \c "too many states for serving".  Gemini's schema is also a subset of JSON Schema without references, free-form
    maps or type alternatives.

    @ref shapeToolParameters() therefore keeps every member of a tool's parameters and declares the rest as JSON text:
    |!Original schema|!Sent to Gemini
    |objects and arrays up to @ref ToolSchemaMaxDepth levels deep, with their members, types, descriptions and \c required lists|unchanged
    |constraint keywords (\c enum, \c default, \c title, lengths, bounds, \c pattern, \c format, \c additionalProperties, ...)|left out; the caller still validates them
    |local \c "$ref" references (\c "#/$defs/...", \c "#/definitions/...", any local JSON pointer)|the referenced schema
    |\c allOf, \c anyOf, \c oneOf alternatives of one type|one schema with the members of all alternatives
    |a \c "null" alternative or type|\c nullable
    |\c const|a one-value \c enum (left out of tool parameters, as other constraints)
    |an object or array nested deeper than @ref ToolSchemaMaxDepth|a string holding JSON text
    |a free-form object (no declared properties, additional properties allowed)|a string holding JSON text
    |a value without a type, or alternatives of different types|a string holding JSON text
    |a recursive or unresolvable reference|a string holding JSON text

    A value sent as JSON text is declared as a string whose description holds the original schema, including the
    schemas that it references.  The providers record which arguments of which tools of a request are JSON text
    (@ref GeminiChatRequest::stringified_arguments) and return tool calls (@ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse::tool_calls,
    and the function calls of streamed chunks) with these values parsed, so tool callers and tool contracts keep the
    original schema.  Tool calls replayed in the conversation history are sent in the declared form.  A request that
    uses cached content should be given the tools of the cache, so that their arguments are decoded.

    @par Example
    A choice dialog keeps the members of its options, and a free-form \c metadata map is sent as JSON text:
    @code{.py}
hash<GeminiToolParameterSchema> shaped = GeminiBodyShape::shapeToolParameters({
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
        "options": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "object", "properties": {
            "label": {"type": "string"}, "value": {"type": "string"}}}},
        "metadata": {"type": "object", "additionalProperties": {"type": "string"}},
    },
});
# shaped.parameters.properties.options.items.properties has "label" and "value"
# shaped.parameters.properties.metadata.type is "string"; shaped.stringified is (("metadata",),)
hash<auto> args = GeminiBodyShape::decodeToolArguments({"options": (), "metadata": "{\"env\":\"prod\"}"},
    shaped.stringified);
# args.metadata is {"env": "prod"}
    @endcode

    @section geminibodyshaperelnotes Release Notes

    @subsection geminibodyshape_v1_0 GeminiBodyShape v1.0
    - initial release
    - Gemini 3.x uses qualitative thinking levels and omits deprecated sampling parameters and numeric budgets;
      Gemini 2.5 retains its existing controls (see @ref geminibodyshapegeneration)
    - explicit prompt caching: @ref shapeChatBody() takes a \c cached_content reference and then leaves out
      \c systemInstruction, \c tools and \c toolConfig, which belong to the cached content
      (@ref shapeCachedContentBody()); providers take it from
      @ref QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions::cached_content "LlmRequestOptions::cached_content"
    - @ref normalizeUsage() marks that thinking tokens are not part of the output tokens
      (\c reasoning_in_output = @ref False) and reports the cached tokens explicitly, as \c 0 for a cache miss
    - tool parameter schemas keep their nested members, so that Gemini can fill nested objects and arrays of objects
      instead of sending \c {}; values that Gemini's schema cannot declare are sent as JSON text and returned to
      callers with their original types (see @ref geminibodyshapetoolschemas)
*/

#! Contains all public definitions in the GeminiBodyShape module
public namespace GeminiBodyShape {
#! The maximum nesting depth of objects and arrays that a Gemini tool parameter schema keeps as structure
/** The root parameters object is at depth 1, an object or array in one of its properties at depth 2, and so on.
    An object or array nested deeper is declared to Gemini as a string holding JSON text (see
    @ref geminibodyshapetoolschemas).

    Google documents no numeric limit; it states only that very large or deeply nested schemas may be rejected,
    which Gemini reports as \c "too many states for serving" because it compiles the function declarations of a
    request into one constrained-decoding state machine.  Values deeper than this limit are still sent and
    returned exactly, as JSON text.
*/
public const ToolSchemaMaxDepth = 5;

#! A Gemini tool parameter schema and the arguments that it declares as JSON strings
/** Returned by @ref shapeToolParameters().

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hashdecl GeminiToolParameterSchema {
    #! The parameter schema to send in the function declaration
    hash<auto> parameters;
    #! The path of each argument value that @ref parameters declares as a string holding JSON text
    /** Each path element is a property name, or @ref nothing for every element of an array; for example
        <tt>("order", "lines", NOTHING, "product")</tt> is the \c product of every element of \c order.lines.
        @ref decodeToolArguments() parses these values back to their declared types.
    */
    list<list<*string>> stringified = ();
}

#! A Gemini \c generateContent request body and the tool arguments that it declares as JSON strings
/** Returned by @ref shapeChatRequest().

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hashdecl GeminiChatRequest {
    #! The request body
    hash<auto> body;
    #! The paths of the stringified arguments of each tool (only tools that have any), by tool name
    /** See @ref GeminiToolParameterSchema::stringified; pass this to @ref parseChatResponse() or
        @ref decodeResponseToolArguments() so that tool calls are returned with their declared argument types.
    */
    hash<string, list<list<*string>>> stringified_arguments = {};
}

#! Returns the Gemini model resource for REST calls
/** Canonicalizes the model name to the form Gemini's REST APIs expect:
    bare names are prefixed with \c "models/"; already-qualified names are
    returned unchanged.

    @param model the configured model name (e.g. \c "gemini-2.0-flash" or
        \c "models/gemini-2.0-flash")

    @return the canonical Gemini model resource path
*/
public string sub modelResource(string model) {
    return model =~ /^models\// ? model : "models/" + model;
}

#! Returns the bare Gemini model name required by streaming helper APIs
/** @param model a canonical or bare Gemini model name

    @return the model name with any leading \c "models/" prefix removed
*/
public string sub bareModelName(string model) {
    return regex_subst(model, "^models/", "");
}

#! Returns a Gemini-compatible copy of a JSON schema
/** Gemini's function declarations and response schemas accept only a
    subset of JSON Schema / OpenAPI.  In particular,
    \c additionalProperties causes \c generateContent to reject the request
    with HTTP 400 even when it is a boolean.  Deep composition and
    value/length constraints can also make Gemini's constrained decoder
    reject a request with "too many states for serving".

    Simplify unsupported or serving-expensive schema keywords at the
    provider boundary so callers can keep using stricter OpenAI/Anthropic
    schemas and local validators: local \c "$ref" references are resolved,
    \c allOf / \c anyOf / \c oneOf alternatives are merged, a \c "null"
    alternative or type becomes \c nullable, and \c const becomes a
    one-value \c enum.

    @param schema the input JSON schema (or @ref nothing)
    @param compact when @ref True, shape the schema as tool parameters with
        @ref shapeToolParameters() and return its \c parameters; use
        @ref shapeToolParameters() directly to also get the arguments that
        are declared as JSON strings

    @return the sanitized schema (or @ref nothing if input was empty)
*/
public *hash<auto> sub sanitizeSchema(*hash<auto> schema, bool compact = False) {
    if (!schema) {
        return NOTHING;
    }
    if (compact) {
        return GeminiBodyShape::shapeToolParameters(schema).parameters;
    }
    GeminiSchemaShaper shaper(schema, False);
    return shaper.shapeRoot();
}

#! Returns the Gemini form of a tool's parameter schema
/** Every member of the schema is kept, so that Gemini's constrained decoder can fill it, and the schema keywords
    that are unsupported or expensive for Gemini's decoder are removed (see @ref geminibodyshapetoolschemas).  A
    value that Gemini's schema cannot declare is declared as a string holding JSON text instead, with the original
    schema in its description:
    - an object or array nested deeper than @ref ToolSchemaMaxDepth
    - a free-form object (one without declared properties that allows additional properties); Gemini can fill only
      the declared properties of an object, so it would always send \c {}
    - a value without a type, or whose alternatives (\c anyOf, \c oneOf, a type list) have different types
    - a recursive or unresolvable \c "$ref" reference

    The returned paths name these values, so that @ref decodeToolArguments() returns tool-call arguments with the
    types of the original schema.

    @param parameters the tool's parameter schema; an empty schema declares no parameters

    @return the schema to send and the paths of the arguments that it declares as JSON strings

    @par Example
    @code{.py}
hash<GeminiToolParameterSchema> shaped = GeminiBodyShape::shapeToolParameters(tool.parameters);
# ... send shaped.parameters, then decode a function call's arguments
hash<auto> args = GeminiBodyShape::decodeToolArguments(function_call.args, shaped.stringified);
    @endcode

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hash<GeminiToolParameterSchema> sub shapeToolParameters(*hash<auto> parameters) {
    if (!parameters) {
        return <GeminiToolParameterSchema>{"parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {}}};
    }
    GeminiSchemaShaper shaper(parameters, True);
    hash<auto> schema = shaper.shapeRoot();
    return <GeminiToolParameterSchema>{
        "parameters": schema,
        "stringified": shaper.getStringified(),
    };
}

#! Returns tool-call arguments with the values that were declared as JSON strings parsed
/** @param args the arguments of a Gemini \c functionCall
    @param stringified the paths of the arguments that the tool declares as JSON strings
        (@ref GeminiToolParameterSchema::stringified)

    @return the arguments with each string value at one of the paths parsed as JSON; a value that is not a string
    (Gemini already sent it structured) or that is not valid JSON is returned unchanged, so that the caller's
    validation reports it

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hash<auto> sub decodeToolArguments(hash<auto> args, *list<list<*string>> stringified) {
    hash<auto> rv = args;
    foreach list<*string> path in (stringified) {
        rv = cast<hash>(GeminiBodyShape::transformToolArgument(rv, path, 0, True));
    }
    return rv;
}

#! Returns tool-call arguments with the values that a tool declares as JSON strings serialized
/** The inverse of @ref decodeToolArguments(), used to replay a previous tool call to Gemini in the form that its
    tool declaration has.

    @param args tool-call arguments with their declared types
    @param stringified the paths of the arguments that the tool declares as JSON strings
        (@ref GeminiToolParameterSchema::stringified)

    @return the arguments with each value at one of the paths serialized as JSON text

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hash<auto> sub encodeToolArguments(hash<auto> args, *list<list<*string>> stringified) {
    hash<auto> rv = args;
    foreach list<*string> path in (stringified) {
        rv = cast<hash>(GeminiBodyShape::transformToolArgument(rv, path, 0, False));
    }
    return rv;
}

#! Returns a Gemini response with the stringified arguments of its function calls decoded
/** Applies @ref decodeToolArguments() to the \c args of every \c functionCall part of every candidate; used for
    streamed responses, whose chunks carry the function calls.

    @param body a \c generateContent response or \c streamGenerateContent chunk
    @param stringified_arguments the paths of the stringified arguments of each tool, by tool name
        (@ref GeminiChatRequest::stringified_arguments)

    @return the response with decoded function-call arguments

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hash<auto> sub decodeResponseToolArguments(hash<auto> body,
        *hash<string, list<list<*string>>> stringified_arguments) {
    if (!stringified_arguments || body.candidates.typeCode() != NT_LIST) {
        return body;
    }
    hash<auto> rv = body;
    list<auto> candidates = ();
    foreach auto cand in (body.candidates) {
        if (cand.typeCode() != NT_HASH || cand.content.parts.typeCode() != NT_LIST) {
            push candidates, cand;
            continue;
        }
        list<auto> parts = ();
        foreach auto part in (cand.content.parts) {
            if (part.typeCode() == NT_HASH && part.functionCall.typeCode() == NT_HASH
                    && part.functionCall.args.typeCode() == NT_HASH
                    && part.functionCall.name.typeCode() == NT_STRING
                    && stringified_arguments{part.functionCall.name}) {
                hash<auto> decoded = cast<hash>(part);
                decoded.functionCall.args = GeminiBodyShape::decodeToolArguments(part.functionCall.args,
                    stringified_arguments{part.functionCall.name});
                push parts, decoded;
            } else {
                push parts, part;
            }
        }
        hash<auto> decoded_cand = cast<hash>(cand);
        decoded_cand.content.parts = parts;
        push candidates, decoded_cand;
    }
    rv.candidates = candidates;
    return rv;
}

#! Applies JSON decoding or encoding to the value at a stringified argument path
auto sub transformToolArgument(auto value, list<*string> path, int idx, bool decode) {
    if (idx == path.size()) {
        if (decode) {
            if (value.typeCode() != NT_STRING) {
                return value;
            }
            try {
                return parse_json(value);
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                # not JSON: return the text so that the caller's validation reports it
                return value;
            }
        }
        return exists value ? make_json(value) : value;
    }
    *string name = path[idx];
    if (!exists name) {
        if (value.typeCode() != NT_LIST) {
            return value;
        }
        list<auto> rv = ();
        foreach auto elem in (value) {
            push rv, GeminiBodyShape::transformToolArgument(elem, path, idx + 1, decode);
        }
        return rv;
    }
    if (value.typeCode() != NT_HASH || !value.hasKey(name)) {
        return value;
    }
    hash<auto> rv = cast<hash>(value);
    rv{name} = GeminiBodyShape::transformToolArgument(rv{name}, path, idx + 1, decode);
    return rv;
}

#! Shapes a JSON schema for Gemini (internal to @ref sanitizeSchema() and @ref shapeToolParameters())
class GeminiSchemaShaper {
    private {
        #! the root schema, against which local references are resolved
        hash<auto> root;
        #! True when shaping tool parameters
        bool tool;
        #! the paths of the values declared as JSON strings
        list<list<*string>> stringified = ();
        #! the references being expanded on the current path, to detect recursion
        hash<string, bool> expanding = {};
    }

    constructor(hash<auto> root, bool tool) {
        self.root = root;
        self.tool = tool;
    }

    #! Returns the shaped root schema
    hash<auto> shapeRoot() {
        auto rv = shape(root, 1, (), False);
        # a hash input is always shaped to a hash: only member positions are stringified
        @assert(rv.typeCode() == NT_HASH);
        return cast<hash>(rv);
    }

    #! Returns the paths of the values declared as JSON strings
    list<list<*string>> getStringified() {
        return stringified;
    }

    #! Shapes one schema value
    /** @param value the schema value
        @param depth the object/array nesting depth of the value (the root is at depth 1)
        @param path the argument path of the value
        @param member True if the value is a property or array element, which can be declared as a JSON string
    */
    private auto shape(auto value, int depth, list<*string> path, bool member) {
        if (value.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
            return value;
        }
        hash<auto> node = cast<hash>(value);

        if (node."$ref".typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
            string ref = node."$ref";
            *hash<auto> target = expanding{ref} ? NOTHING : resolveRef(ref);
            if (!exists target) {
                if (tool && member) {
                    return stringify(node, path, False);
                }
                # Gemini has no references: an unresolvable one is dropped
                remove node."$ref";
            } else {
                expanding{ref} = True;
                on_exit remove expanding{ref};
                # sibling keywords (e.g. a description) refine the referenced schema
                return shape(target + (node - "$ref"), depth, path, member);
            }
        }

        if (node.hasKey("const")) {
            if (!node.hasKey("enum")) {
                node."enum" = (node."const",);
            }
            remove node."const";
        }

        bool nullable = False;
        bool type_conflict = False;
        list<string> variant_refs = ();
        if (node.allOf.typeCode() == NT_LIST || node.anyOf.typeCode() == NT_LIST
                || node.oneOf.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
            node = mergeComposition(node, \nullable, \type_conflict, \variant_refs);
        }
        # references expanded in the alternatives are being expanded until this value is shaped
        foreach string ref in (variant_refs) {
            expanding{ref} = True;
        }
        on_exit {
            foreach string ref in (variant_refs) {
                remove expanding{ref};
            }
        }

        if (node.type.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
            list<string> types = ();
            foreach auto type in (node.type) {
                if (type == "null") {
                    nullable = True;
                } else if (type.typeCode() == NT_STRING && !types.contains(type)) {
                    types += type;
                }
            }
            if (types.size() == 1) {
                node.type = types[0];
            } else if (!types) {
                remove node.type;
            } else {
                type_conflict = True;
            }
        }
        if (nullable) {
            node.nullable = True;
        }
        if (!exists node.type) {
            *string type = GeminiSchemaShaper::inferType(node);
            if (type) {
                node.type = type;
            }
        }

        if (tool && member
                && (type_conflict
                    || node.type.typeCode() != NT_STRING
                    || GeminiSchemaShaper::isFreeFormObject(node)
                    || (depth > GeminiBodyShape::ToolSchemaMaxDepth
                        && (node.type == "object" || node.type == "array")))) {
            return stringify(cast<hash>(value), path, nullable);
        }

        hash<auto> rv = {};
        foreach string key in (keys node) {
            if (GeminiBodyShape::isSchemaKeywordStripped(key)
                    || GeminiBodyShape::isSchemaMetadataKeyword(key)
                    || (tool && GeminiBodyShape::isCompactSchemaKeywordStripped(key))
                    || GeminiBodyShape::isSchemaCompositionKeyword(key)) {
                continue;
            }
            # "properties" and "patternProperties" are name->schema maps:
            # their keys are caller-defined field names (or patterns), not
            # schema keywords, so they must pass through verbatim while only
            # the mapped schema values are shaped.  Treating them as an
            # ordinary schema object would drop any property whose name
            # collides with a stripped keyword (e.g. a field literally named
            # "name", "format", or "enum").
            if (key == "properties" && node.properties.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
                # {} (not unassigned): a no-argument tool's "properties": {} must stay an empty map
                hash<auto> props = {};
                foreach hash<auto> i in (node.properties.pairIterator()) {
                    list<*string> member_path = path;
                    push member_path, i.key;
                    props{i.key} = shape(i.value, depth + 1, member_path, True);
                }
                rv.properties = props;
                continue;
            }
            if (key == "patternProperties" && node.patternProperties.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
                hash<auto> props = {};
                foreach hash<auto> i in (node.patternProperties.pairIterator()) {
                    props{i.key} = shape(i.value, depth + 1, path, False);
                }
                rv.patternProperties = props;
                continue;
            }
            if (key == "items" && node.items.typeCode() == NT_HASH && node.items) {
                list<*string> item_path = path;
                push item_path, NOTHING;
                rv.items = shape(node.items, depth + 1, item_path, True);
                continue;
            }
            rv{key} = shapeOther(node{key}, depth);
        }
        # An unconstrained array is legal JSON Schema and is commonly
        # produced for Qore softlist<auto> data-provider fields as
        # {"type":"array","items":{}}.  Gemini's protobuf-backed Schema
        # treats that empty child message like an absent field and rejects
        # the complete function catalog with INVALID_ARGUMENT.  Keep the
        # provider-neutral schema permissive and apply the same conservative
        # string-item fallback used by QoreLlmUtils at this provider boundary.
        if (rv.type == "array"
                && (rv.items.typeCode() != NT_HASH || !rv.items)) {
            rv.items = {"type": "string"};
        }
        return rv;
    }

    #! Shapes the value of a keyword that is not a name->schema map; nested schemas are not argument values
    private auto shapeOther(auto value, int depth) {
        if (value.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            return shape(value, depth + 1, (), False);
        }
        if (value.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
            list<auto> rv = ();
            foreach auto item in (value) {
                push rv, shapeOther(item, depth);
            }
            return rv;
        }
        return value;
    }

    #! Merges allOf / anyOf / oneOf alternatives into one schema
    private hash<auto> mergeComposition(hash<auto> node, reference<bool> nullable, reference<bool> type_conflict,
            reference<list<string>> variant_refs) {
        hash<auto> rv = node - ("allOf", "anyOf", "oneOf");
        hash<string, bool> types = {};
        if (rv.type.typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
            types{rv.type} = True;
        }
        foreach string key in (("allOf", "anyOf", "oneOf")) {
            if (node{key}.typeCode() != NT_LIST) {
                continue;
            }
            list<hash<auto>> variants = ();
            foreach auto raw in (node{key}) {
                if (raw.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
                    continue;
                }
                hash<auto> variant = cast<hash>(raw);
                if (variant."$ref".typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
                    string ref = variant."$ref";
                    *hash<auto> target = expanding{ref} || variant_refs.contains(ref) ? NOTHING : resolveRef(ref);
                    if (!exists target) {
                        # the alternative cannot be declared
                        type_conflict = True;
                        continue;
                    }
                    variant_refs += ref;
                    variant = target + (variant - "$ref");
                }
                if (variant.type == "null") {
                    nullable = True;
                    continue;
                }
                if (variant.type.typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
                    types{variant.type} = True;
                }
                variants += variant;
            }
            if (!variants) {
                continue;
            }
            hash<auto> base = rv;
            foreach hash<auto> variant in (variants) {
                rv = GeminiBodyShape::mergeSchemaObjects(rv, variant);
            }
            if (tool) {
                remove rv.required;
            } else {
                list<string> required = GeminiBodyShape::mergeRequiredLists(
                    GeminiBodyShape::schemaStringList(base.required),
                    GeminiBodyShape::compositionRequiredFields(variants, key == "allOf"));
                if (required) {
                    rv.required = required;
                } else {
                    remove rv.required;
                }
            }
        }
        if (types.size() > 1) {
            type_conflict = True;
        }
        return rv;
    }

    #! Returns a string schema whose description holds the original schema, and records the value's path
    private hash<auto> stringify(hash<auto> node, list<*string> path, bool nullable) {
        push stringified, path;
        string desc;
        if (node.description.typeCode() == NT_STRING && node.description.val()) {
            desc = node.description + "\n\n";
        }
        desc += "This value is a string holding JSON text (not an object or list) that matches this JSON schema: "
            + make_json(node - ("description", "$schema", "$id", "$comment", "$defs", "definitions"));
        hash<string, hash<auto>> defs = {};
        collectReferences(node, \defs);
        if (defs) {
            desc += "\nThe schemas that it references with \"$ref\": " + make_json(defs);
        }
        hash<auto> rv = {
            "type": "string",
            "description": desc,
        };
        if (nullable) {
            rv.nullable = True;
        }
        return rv;
    }

    #! Collects the local schemas that a schema references, transitively
    private collectReferences(auto value, reference<hash<string, hash<auto>>> defs) {
        if (value.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
            foreach auto item in (value) {
                collectReferences(item, \defs);
            }
            return;
        }
        if (value.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
            return;
        }
        foreach hash<auto> i in (value.pairIterator()) {
            if (i.key == "$ref" && i.value.typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
                string ref = i.value;
                if (defs{ref}) {
                    continue;
                }
                *hash<auto> target = resolveRef(ref);
                if (target) {
                    hash<auto> def = target - ("$defs", "definitions");
                    defs{ref} = def;
                    collectReferences(def, \defs);
                }
                continue;
            }
            collectReferences(i.value, \defs);
        }
    }

    #! Resolves a local JSON pointer reference (\c "#" or \c "#/...") against the root schema
    private *hash<auto> resolveRef(string ref) {
        if (ref == "#") {
            return root;
        }
        if (ref !~ /^#\//) {
            return NOTHING;
        }
        auto cur = root;
        foreach string seg in (ref.substr(2).split("/")) {
            # JSON pointer escapes (RFC 6901)
            seg = replace(replace(seg, "~1", "/"), "~0", "~");
            if (cur.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
                if (!cur.hasKey(seg)) {
                    return NOTHING;
                }
                cur = cur{seg};
            } else if (cur.typeCode() == NT_LIST && seg =~ /^[0-9]+$/) {
                cur = cur[seg.toInt()];
            } else {
                return NOTHING;
            }
        }
        return cur.typeCode() == NT_HASH ? cast<hash>(cur) : NOTHING;
    }

    #! Returns the type of a schema without one, if its keywords determine it
    private static *string inferType(hash<auto> node) {
        if (node.properties.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            return "object";
        }
        if (node.hasKey("items")) {
            return "array";
        }
        if (node."enum".typeCode() == NT_LIST && node."enum") {
            hash<string, bool> types = {};
            foreach auto v in (node."enum") {
                switch (v.typeCode()) {
                    case NT_STRING: types.string = True; break;
                    case NT_INT: types.integer = True; break;
                    case NT_FLOAT:
                    case NT_NUMBER: types.number = True; break;
                    case NT_BOOLEAN: types.boolean = True; break;
                    default: return NOTHING;
                }
            }
            if (types.size() == 1) {
                return types.firstKey();
            }
            if (types.size() == 2 && types.integer && types.number) {
                return "number";
            }
        }
        return NOTHING;
    }

    #! True for an object without declared properties that allows additional properties
    private static bool isFreeFormObject(hash<auto> node) {
        if (node.type != "object") {
            return False;
        }
        if (node.properties.typeCode() == NT_HASH && node.properties) {
            return False;
        }
        # an object closed to additional properties can only be {}, which Gemini can fill
        return node.additionalProperties !== False;
    }
}

bool sub isSchemaCompositionKeyword(string key) {
    switch (key) {
        case "allOf":
        case "anyOf":
        case "oneOf":
            return True;
    }
    return False;
}

#! True for JSON-Schema dialect/labelling keywords Gemini's schema rejects
/** Gemini's \c responseSchema and tool \c parameters accept an OpenAPI 3.0
    Schema subset that has no notion of these JSON-Schema dialect or
    labelling keywords; sending them yields an \c INVALID_ARGUMENT (HTTP
    400) "Unknown name" error (e.g. a stray top-level \c "name" on a
    structured-output schema).  These are stripped only at schema-object
    positions — never from \c properties keys — so a field literally named
    \c "name" is preserved.

    @param key the schema-object key under consideration

    @return @ref True if the key is a non-schema metadata keyword to drop
*/
bool sub isSchemaMetadataKeyword(string key) {
    switch (key) {
        case "name":
        case "$schema":
        case "$id":
        case "$ref":
        case "$comment":
        case "$defs":
        case "definitions":
            return True;
    }
    return False;
}

bool sub isSchemaKeywordStripped(string key) {
    switch (key) {
        case "additionalProperties":
        case "allowed_values":
        case "default_value":
        case "example_value":
        case "minLength":
        case "maxLength":
        case "pattern":
        case "format":
        case "minimum":
        case "maximum":
        case "exclusiveMinimum":
        case "exclusiveMaximum":
        case "minItems":
        case "maxItems":
        case "minProperties":
        case "maxProperties":
        case "multipleOf":
        case "position":
        case "positional":
        case "sensitive":
        case "uniqueItems":
            return True;
    }
    return False;
}

#! True for the keywords that tool parameter schemas leave out to keep Gemini's decoder small
/** These constrain values rather than declare members; the constrained decoder enumerates their states for every
    function declaration of the request.
*/
bool sub isCompactSchemaKeywordStripped(string key) {
    switch (key) {
        case "default":
        case "enum":
        case "title":
            return True;
    }
    return False;
}

hash<auto> sub mergeSchemaObjects(hash<auto> left, hash<auto> right) {
    hash<auto> rv = left;

    if (exists right.type) {
        if (!exists rv.type) {
            rv.type = right.type;
        } else if (make_json(rv.type) != make_json(right.type)) {
            remove rv.type;
        }
    }

    if (right{"enum"}.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
        rv{"enum"} = GeminiBodyShape::mergeEnumLists(rv{"enum"},
            right{"enum"});
    }

    if (right.items.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
        if (rv.items.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            rv.items = GeminiBodyShape::mergeSchemaObjects(
                cast<hash>(rv.items),
                cast<hash>(right.items));
        } else {
            rv.items = right.items;
        }
    }

    if (right.properties.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
        hash<auto> props = rv.properties.typeCode() == NT_HASH
            ? cast<hash>(rv.properties) : {};
        hash<auto> right_props = cast<hash>(right.properties);
        foreach string key in (keys right_props) {
            if (exists props{key}
                    && props{key}.typeCode() == NT_HASH
                    && right_props{key}.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
                props{key} = GeminiBodyShape::mergeSchemaObjects(
                    cast<hash>(props{key}),
                    cast<hash>(right_props{key}));
            } else if (!exists props{key}) {
                props{key} = right_props{key};
            }
        }
        rv.properties = props;
    }

    return rv;
}

list<string> sub compositionRequiredFields(list<hash<auto>> variants,
        bool all_required) {
    hash<string, bool> out = {};
    bool initialized = False;
    foreach hash<auto> variant in (variants) {
        list<string> required = GeminiBodyShape::schemaStringList(
            variant.required);
        hash<string, bool> current = GeminiBodyShape::stringSet(required);
        if (!initialized) {
            out = current;
            initialized = True;
            continue;
        }
        if (all_required) {
            foreach string key in (keys current) {
                out{key} = True;
            }
        } else {
            foreach string key in (keys out) {
                if (!exists current{key}) {
                    remove out{key};
                }
            }
        }
    }
    return GeminiBodyShape::sortedStringKeys(out);
}

list<string> sub mergeRequiredLists(list<string> left, list<string> right) {
    hash<string, bool> seen = GeminiBodyShape::stringSet(left);
    foreach string key in (right) {
        seen{key} = True;
    }
    return GeminiBodyShape::sortedStringKeys(seen);
}

hash<string, bool> sub stringSet(list<string> values) {
    hash<string, bool> rv = {};
    foreach string value in (values) {
        rv{value} = True;
    }
    return rv;
}

list<string> sub sortedStringKeys(hash<string, bool> values) {
    if (!values) {
        return ();
    }
    return sort(keys values, int sub (string l, string r) {
        return l == r ? 0 : (l < r ? -1 : 1);
    });
}

list<string> sub schemaStringList(auto value) {
    list<string> rv = ();
    if (value.typeCode() != NT_LIST) {
        return rv;
    }
    foreach auto item in (value) {
        rv += item.toString();
    }
    return rv;
}

list<auto> sub mergeEnumLists(auto left, auto right) {
    list<auto> rv = ();
    hash<string, bool> seen = {};
    foreach auto item in (GeminiBodyShape::schemaList(left)
            + GeminiBodyShape::schemaList(right)) {
        string key = make_json(item);
        if (!seen{key}) {
            seen{key} = True;
            rv += item;
        }
    }
    return rv;
}

list<auto> sub schemaList(auto value) {
    if (value.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
        return cast<list>(value);
    }
    return ();
}

#! Builds Gemini content parts from a generic @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage
/** Multimodal messages (when \c content_parts is populated) become
    \c inlineData parts; text-only messages become a single \c text part.

    @param msg the source chat message

    @return a list of Gemini-shaped content-part hashes (may be empty)
*/
public list<hash<auto>> sub shapeContentParts(hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage> msg) {
    list<hash<auto>> parts = ();
    if (msg.content_parts) {
        foreach hash<QoreLlmUtils::ContentPart> part in (msg.content_parts) {
            if (part.type == "image" && part.data) {
                push parts, {
                    "inlineData": {
                        "mimeType": part.mime_type ?? "image/png",
                        "data": make_base64_string(part.data),
                    },
                };
            } else if (part.type == "file" && part.data) {
                push parts, {
                    "inlineData": {
                        "mimeType": part.mime_type
                            ?? "application/octet-stream",
                        "data": make_base64_string(part.data),
                    },
                };
            } else if (part.type == "text" && part.text.val()) {
                push parts, {"text": part.text};
            }
        }
    } else if (msg.content.val()) {
        push parts, {"text": msg.content};
    }
    return parts;
}

#! Parses an OpenAI-style tool-result string into Gemini \c functionResponse.response
/** OpenAI-style tool results are typically JSON strings; Gemini expects
    a hash.  Parse the JSON when possible; on parse failure, wrap the raw
    content under a \c "result" key so the model still receives the data.

    @param content the OpenAI-style tool result string

    @return a hash suitable for Gemini's \c functionResponse.response
*/
public hash<auto> sub parseToolResponse(*string content) {
    if (!content.val()) {
        return {};
    }
    try {
        auto parsed = parse_json(content);
        return parsed.typeCode() == NT_HASH
            ? cast<hash>(parsed)
            : {"result": parsed};
    } catch () {
        return {"result": content};
    }
}

#! Returns whether a model belongs to the Gemini 3 family
/** @param model a bare model ID or a Gemini/Vertex model resource name
    @return @ref True for Gemini 3.x, @ref False for older or unknown models
*/
public bool sub usesThinkingLevel(string model) {
    model =~ s/^.*\///;
    return model =~ /^gemini-3([.-]|$)/;
}

#! Applies Gemini 3 generation-parameter compatibility rules after all body overrides
/** Removes deprecated sampling parameters and numeric thinking budgets for Gemini 3.x.
    Other model families retain their existing request body. Both REST camelCase names and protobuf
    snake_case aliases are handled. A supplied thinking level is normalized to uppercase.

    @param model the selected model ID or resource name
    @param body the complete request body, including provider-specific overrides
    @return the normalized request body; the caller's hash is not modified
    @throw GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR configuration objects or thinking levels are invalid, or both
        spellings of a configuration object are supplied
    @note Numeric budgets have no exact level equivalent and are omitted on Gemini 3.x, including zero
        and the dynamic budget -1. Supply an explicit thinking level to override the model default.
        Supported levels depend on the model; Gemini 3.x cannot fully disable thinking.

    @par Example
    A support-ticket classifier can request low reasoning effort while allowing the model to manage sampling:
    @code{.py}
hash<auto> body = GeminiBodyShape::normalizeGenerationConfig("gemini-3.1-pro-preview", {
    "generationConfig": {"thinkingConfig": {"thinkingLevel": "low"}},
});
    @endcode
*/
public hash<auto> sub normalizeGenerationConfig(string model, hash<auto> body) {
    if (!usesThinkingLevel(model)) {
        return body;
    }
    if (exists body.generationConfig && exists body.generation_config) {
        throw "GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR", "use only one of generationConfig and generation_config";
    }
    auto config = remove body.generation_config ?? body.generationConfig;
    if (config.typeCode() == NT_NOTHING) {
        return body;
    }
    if (config.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
        throw "GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR", "generationConfig must be a hash";
    }
    hash<auto> gen = cast<hash>(config) - ("temperature", "topP", "topK", "top_p", "top_k");
    if (exists gen.thinkingConfig && exists gen.thinking_config) {
        throw "GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR", "use only one of thinkingConfig and thinking_config";
    }
    auto thinking = remove gen.thinking_config ?? gen.thinkingConfig;
    if (thinking.typeCode() != NT_NOTHING) {
        if (thinking.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
            throw "GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR", "thinkingConfig must be a hash";
        }
        hash<auto> tc = cast<hash>(thinking) - ("thinkingBudget", "thinking_budget");
        if (exists tc.thinkingLevel && exists tc.thinking_level) {
            throw "GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR", "use only one of thinkingLevel and thinking_level";
        }
        auto level = remove tc.thinking_level ?? tc.thinkingLevel;
        if (level.typeCode() != NT_NOTHING) {
            if (level.typeCode() != NT_STRING || !("MINIMAL", "LOW", "MEDIUM", "HIGH").contains(toupper(level))) {
                throw "GEMINI-GENERATION-CONFIG-ERROR", "thinkingLevel must be minimal, low, medium, or high";
            }
            tc.thinkingLevel = toupper(level);
        }
        if (tc) {
            gen.thinkingConfig = tc;
        } else {
            delete gen.thinkingConfig;
        }
    }
    body.generationConfig = gen;
    return body;
}

#! Builds a Gemini \c generateContent request body from generic chat inputs
/** Returns the \c body of @ref shapeChatRequest(); use @ref shapeChatRequest() to also get the tool arguments
    that the request declares as JSON strings, which a response's tool calls need to be decoded.

    @param messages provider-neutral chat history
    @param tools optional tool definitions
    @param output_schema optional JSON schema for structured output
    @param resolved already-resolved per-call knobs; see @ref shapeChatRequest()

    @return the Gemini-shaped request body
*/
public hash<auto> sub shapeChatBody(list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>> messages,
        *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition>> tools,
        *hash<auto> output_schema,
        hash<auto> resolved) {
    return GeminiBodyShape::shapeChatRequest(messages, tools, output_schema, resolved).body;
}

#! Builds a Gemini \c generateContent request from generic chat inputs
/** Counterpart to the legacy \c buildGeminiBody private instance method.
    The function is pure-static; callers resolve their request-option
    knobs (max output tokens, temperature, reasoning budget, body merge)
    on the host provider and pass the resolved values in via \a resolved.

    @note Contiguous OpenAI-style \c tool result messages are emitted as
    \c functionResponse parts in one Gemini user turn.  Gemini requires
    that turn to contain exactly one response for every function call in
    the preceding model turn.  When a result omits its function name, the
    shaper recovers it from the preceding call's stable id.

    @par Example
    An operations assistant can request service status and alert details in
    parallel.  Passing the two resulting \c tool messages after the assistant
    call turn produces one Gemini user turn containing both responses.

    @param messages provider-neutral chat history
    @param tools optional tool definitions
    @param output_schema optional JSON schema for structured output
    @param resolved already-resolved per-call knobs:
        - \c model (\c *string): selected model; enables Gemini 3.x parameter normalization
        - \c max_output_tokens (\c int): mapped to \c generationConfig.maxOutputTokens
        - \c temperature (\c float): mapped to \c generationConfig.temperature
        - \c reasoning_token_budget (\c *int): mapped to
          \c generationConfig.thinkingConfig.thinkingBudget for models before Gemini 3
        - \c reasoning_effort (\c *string): Gemini 3.x \c thinkingLevel; \c xhigh and \c max map to \c HIGH
        - \c extra_body (<tt>*hash&lt;auto&gt;</tt>): merged into the final body so
          callers can pass through provider-specific knobs without
          modifying this shaper
        - \c cached_content (\c *string): the name of a cached content resource
          (\c cachedContents/... for the Gemini API, or
          \c projects/.../locations/.../cachedContents/... for Vertex AI); when set,
          the body references it in \c cachedContent and leaves out
          \c systemInstruction, \c tools and \c toolConfig, which must be part of
          the cached content instead (see @ref applyCachedContent()); system
          messages are therefore not sent

    Tool parameter schemas are shaped with @ref shapeToolParameters(); the arguments of the assistant tool calls
    in \a messages are replayed in the shaped form (see @ref encodeToolArguments()).

    @return the Gemini-shaped request body and the paths of the arguments that each tool declares as JSON strings;
    pass \c stringified_arguments to @ref parseChatResponse() or @ref decodeResponseToolArguments()

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public hash<GeminiChatRequest> sub shapeChatRequest(list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>> messages,
        *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition>> tools,
        *hash<auto> output_schema,
        hash<auto> resolved) {
    # tools are shaped first: replayed tool calls take the shape of their declarations
    list<hash<auto>> declarations = ();
    hash<string, list<list<*string>>> stringified_arguments = {};
    foreach hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition> td in (tools) {
        hash<GeminiToolParameterSchema> shaped = GeminiBodyShape::shapeToolParameters(td.parameters);
        push declarations, {
            "name": td.name,
            "description": td.description ?? "",
            "parameters": shaped.parameters,
        };
        if (shaped.stringified) {
            stringified_arguments{td.name} = shaped.stringified;
        }
    }

    list<hash<auto>> contents = ();
    list<hash<auto>> system_parts = ();
    list<hash<auto>> tool_response_parts = ();
    hash<string, string> tool_call_names;

    foreach hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage> msg in (messages) {
        if (msg.role != "tool" && tool_response_parts) {
            push contents, {"role": "user", "parts": tool_response_parts};
            tool_response_parts = ();
        }
        if (msg.role == "system") {
            list<hash<auto>> parts = GeminiBodyShape::shapeContentParts(msg);
            if (parts) {
                system_parts += parts;
            }
            continue;
        }

        list<hash<auto>> parts;
        if (msg.role == "tool") {
            push tool_response_parts, {
                "functionResponse": {
                    "name": msg.name
                        ?? tool_call_names{msg.tool_call_id}
                        ?? msg.tool_call_id
                        ?? "tool_result",
                    "response": GeminiBodyShape::parseToolResponse(msg.content),
                },
            };
            continue;
        }

        parts = GeminiBodyShape::shapeContentParts(msg);
        if (msg.role == "assistant" && msg.tool_calls) {
            tool_call_names = {};
            foreach hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatToolCall> tc in (msg.tool_calls) {
                if (tc.id.val() && tc.name.val()) {
                    tool_call_names{tc.id} = tc.name;
                }
                hash<auto!> part = {
                    "functionCall": {
                        "name": tc.name,
                        "args": GeminiBodyShape::encodeToolArguments(tc.arguments ?? {},
                            stringified_arguments{tc.name}),
                    },
                };
                # Gemini 3.x rejects a replayed function call whose reasoning signature is missing,
                # so echo back verbatim the signature returned with the original call
                if (tc.thought_signature.val()) {
                    part.thoughtSignature = tc.thought_signature;
                }
                push parts, part;
            }
        }
        if (!parts) {
            parts = ({"text": msg.content ?? ""},);
        }
        push contents, {
            "role": msg.role == "assistant" ? "model" : "user",
            "parts": parts,
        };
    }
    if (tool_response_parts) {
        push contents, {"role": "user", "parts": tool_response_parts};
    }

    hash<auto!> body;
    body.contents = contents;
    if (system_parts) {
        body.systemInstruction = {"parts": system_parts};
    }

    hash<auto!> generation_config = {
        "maxOutputTokens": resolved.max_output_tokens,
        "temperature": resolved.temperature,
    };
    if (usesThinkingLevel(resolved.model ?? "") && resolved.reasoning_effort.typeCode() != NT_NOTHING) {
        string effort = toupper(resolved.reasoning_effort);
        generation_config.thinkingConfig = {
            "thinkingLevel": ("XHIGH", "MAX").contains(effort) ? "HIGH" : effort,
        };
    } else if (exists resolved.reasoning_token_budget
            && resolved.reasoning_token_budget.typeCode() != NT_NOTHING) {
        generation_config.thinkingConfig = {
            "thinkingBudget": resolved.reasoning_token_budget,
        };
    }
    if (output_schema) {
        generation_config.responseMimeType = "application/json";
        generation_config.responseSchema = GeminiBodyShape::sanitizeSchema(
            output_schema);
    }
    body.generationConfig = generation_config;

    if (declarations) {
        body.tools = ({"functionDeclarations": declarations},);
    }

    if (resolved.extra_body.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
        body += normalizeGenerationConfig(resolved.model ?? "", resolved.extra_body);
    }
    body = normalizeGenerationConfig(resolved.model ?? "", body);
    if (resolved.cached_content.val()) {
        body = GeminiBodyShape::applyCachedContent(body, resolved.cached_content);
    }
    return <GeminiChatRequest>{
        "body": body,
        "stringified_arguments": stringified_arguments,
    };
}

#! Makes a request body use a cached content resource
/** A request that uses cached content must not repeat the parts of the request that the cache holds: Gemini and
    Vertex AI reject a request with \c cachedContent that also has \c systemInstruction, \c tools or
    \c toolConfig, so they are removed and must be given when the cache is created
    (see @ref shapeCachedContentBody()).

    @param body a \c generateContent request body
    @param cached_content the cached content resource name

    @return the body with \c cachedContent set and without \c systemInstruction, \c tools and \c toolConfig
*/
public hash<auto> sub applyCachedContent(hash<auto> body, string cached_content) {
    return body - ("systemInstruction", "tools", "toolConfig") + {"cachedContent": cached_content};
}

#! Options for creating a cached content resource with @ref shapeCachedContentBody()
public hashdecl GeminiCachedContentOptions {
    #! Time to live in seconds; the server default (one hour) applies if neither this nor \c expire_time is set
    *int ttl_seconds;
    #! Absolute expiration time; mutually exclusive with \c ttl_seconds
    *date expire_time;
    #! Optional display name for the cached content
    *string display_name;
    #! Optional Gemini \c toolConfig for the cached tools (ex: <tt>{"functionCallingConfig": {"mode": "AUTO"}}</tt>)
    *hash<auto> tool_config;
}

#! Returns the expiration fields of a cached content resource
/** @param ttl_seconds the time to live in seconds
    @param expire_time the absolute expiration time

    @return \c ttl as a duration string (ex: \c "3600s") or \c expireTime as an RFC 3339 UTC timestamp, or an
    empty hash if neither is given

    @throw GEMINI-CACHE-ERROR both values are given, or the time to live is not positive
*/
public hash<auto> sub shapeCacheExpiration(*int ttl_seconds, *date expire_time) {
    if (exists ttl_seconds && exists expire_time) {
        throw "GEMINI-CACHE-ERROR", "a cached content expiration takes either a time to live or an expiration "
            "time, not both";
    }
    if (exists ttl_seconds) {
        if (ttl_seconds <= 0) {
            throw "GEMINI-CACHE-ERROR", sprintf("the cached content time to live must be positive; got %d",
                ttl_seconds);
        }
        return {"ttl": sprintf("%ds", ttl_seconds)};
    }
    if (exists expire_time) {
        return {"expireTime": gmtime(expire_time).format("YYYY-MM-DDTHH:mm:SS.xxZ")};
    }
    return {};
}

#! Builds the body of a request that creates a cached content resource
/** The cached content holds the parts of a request that do not change between calls: the system instruction,
    the tools and their configuration, and the leading conversation contents.  Requests then reference it with
    \c cached_content (see @ref shapeChatBody()) instead of sending those parts again.

    The messages are shaped as with @ref shapeChatBody(): system messages become \c systemInstruction and the
    other messages become \c contents.

    @par Example
    @code{.py}
hash<auto> body = GeminiBodyShape::shapeCachedContentBody(
    "projects/my-project/locations/us-central1/publishers/google/models/gemini-2.5-flash",
    (<ChatMessage>{"role": "system", "content": policy_text},
     <ChatMessage>{"role": "user", "content": contract_text}),
    tools, <GeminiCachedContentOptions>{"ttl_seconds": 3600});
    @endcode

    @param model the model resource name (\c models/... for the Gemini API, or
        \c projects/.../locations/.../publishers/google/models/... for Vertex AI)
    @param messages the messages to cache
    @param tools optional tool definitions to cache
    @param opts optional expiration, display name and tool configuration

    @return the \c cachedContents create request body

    @throw GEMINI-CACHE-ERROR invalid expiration options
*/
public hash<auto> sub shapeCachedContentBody(string model, list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>> messages,
        *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition>> tools, *hash<GeminiCachedContentOptions> opts) {
    hash<auto> shaped = GeminiBodyShape::shapeChatBody(messages, tools, NOTHING, {});
    hash<auto!> body = {"model": model};
    if (shaped.contents) {
        body.contents = shaped.contents;
    }
    if (shaped.systemInstruction) {
        body.systemInstruction = shaped.systemInstruction;
    }
    if (shaped.tools) {
        body.tools = shaped.tools;
    }
    if (opts.tool_config) {
        body.toolConfig = opts.tool_config;
    }
    if (opts.display_name.val()) {
        body.displayName = opts.display_name;
    }
    body += GeminiBodyShape::shapeCacheExpiration(opts.ttl_seconds, opts.expire_time);
    return body;
}

#! Parses a Gemini response into a generic @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse
/** @param body the response body
    @param cache_requested @ref True if the request used cached content; see @ref normalizeUsage()
    @param stringified_arguments the paths of the arguments that each tool of the request declares as JSON strings
        (@ref GeminiChatRequest::stringified_arguments); tool calls are returned with these arguments decoded
        (@ref decodeToolArguments()), while \c raw keeps the response as received
*/
public hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse> sub parseChatResponse(hash<auto> body, *bool cache_requested,
        *hash<string, list<list<*string>>> stringified_arguments) {
    hash<auto> cand = body.candidates[0] ?? {};
    list<string> text_parts = ();
    *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatToolCall>> tool_calls;
    int tc_index;
    foreach hash<auto> part in (cand.content.parts ?? ()) {
        if (part.text.val()) {
            push text_parts, part.text;
        } else if (part.functionCall) {
            if (!tool_calls) {
                tool_calls = ();
            }
            # the reasoning signature is a sibling of `functionCall` on the part, not a member of
            # it; it must be carried through and echoed back on the replayed call
            push tool_calls, <QoreLlmUtils::ChatToolCall>{
                "id": part.functionCall.id ?? sprintf("gemini-tool-%d",
                    ++tc_index),
                "name": part.functionCall.name,
                "arguments": GeminiBodyShape::decodeToolArguments(part.functionCall.args ?? {},
                    stringified_arguments{part.functionCall.name}),
                "thought_signature": part.thoughtSignature.typeCode() == NT_STRING
                    ? part.thoughtSignature
                    : NOTHING,
            };
        }
    }

    return <QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse>{
        "id": body.responseId ?? body.id,
        "model": body.model,
        # a blocked prompt has no candidates
        "stop_reason": tool_calls
            ? "tool_use"
            : (!cand.finishReason.val() && body.promptFeedback.blockReason.val())
                ? "content_filter"
                : GeminiBodyShape::mapFinishReason(cand.finishReason),
        "content": text_parts ? text_parts.join("") : NOTHING,
        "tool_calls": tool_calls,
        "usage": GeminiBodyShape::normalizeUsage(body.usageMetadata, cache_requested),
        "raw": body,
        "provider_diagnostics": GeminiBodyShape::providerDiagnostics(body, cand),
    };
}

#! Extracts Gemini-specific diagnostics for provider-neutral callers
public *hash<auto> sub providerDiagnostics(hash<auto> body, hash<auto> cand) {
    hash<auto!> rv;
    int candidate_count = body.candidates.typeCode() == NT_LIST
        ? body.candidates.size() : 0;
    int part_count = cand.content.parts.typeCode() == NT_LIST
        ? cand.content.parts.size() : 0;
    int text_part_count = 0;
    int function_call_count = 0;
    int other_part_count = 0;
    foreach auto raw_part in (cand.content.parts ?? ()) {
        if (raw_part.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
            ++other_part_count;
            continue;
        }
        hash<auto> part = cast<hash>(raw_part);
        if (part.functionCall.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            ++function_call_count;
        } else if (part.text.typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
            ++text_part_count;
        } else {
            ++other_part_count;
        }
    }
    # These wire-shape counters deliberately contain no prompt, generated
    # text, function names, or arguments.  They let callers distinguish a
    # provider response with no function call from an adapter that lost one
    # while normalizing the Gemini envelope.
    rv.wire_protocol = "gemini_generate_content";
    rv.wire_candidate_count = candidate_count;
    rv.wire_part_count = part_count;
    rv.wire_text_part_count = text_part_count;
    rv.wire_function_call_count = function_call_count;
    rv.wire_other_part_count = other_part_count;
    rv.wire_text_observed = text_part_count > 0;
    rv.wire_function_call_observed = function_call_count > 0;
    if (body.responseId.val()) {
        rv.response_id = body.responseId;
    }
    if (body.promptFeedback.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
        rv.prompt_feedback = body.promptFeedback;
    }
    if (body.usageMetadata.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
        rv.usage_metadata = body.usageMetadata;
    }
    if (cand.finishReason.val()) {
        rv.finish_reason = cand.finishReason;
    }
    if (cand.finishMessage.val()) {
        rv.finish_message = cand.finishMessage;
    }
    if (cand.safetyRatings.typeCode() == NT_LIST) {
        rv.safety_ratings = cand.safetyRatings;
    }
    return rv ? rv : NOTHING;
}

#! Extracts text parts from a Gemini response/chunk
public string sub extractText(hash<auto> body) {
    list<string> parts = ();
    foreach hash<auto> part in (body.candidates[0].content.parts ?? ()) {
        if (part.text.val()) {
            push parts, part.text;
        }
    }
    return parts.join("");
}

#! Maps Gemini usage metadata to the OpenAI-style counters
/** Gemini reports its thinking tokens (\c thoughtsTokenCount) separately from the generated output
    (\c candidatesTokenCount), unlike OpenAI, whose reasoning tokens are part of its completion count.  The
    result therefore always has \c reasoning_in_output set to @ref False, and \c reasoning_tokens holds the
    thinking tokens, which are not part of \c completion_tokens / \c output_tokens; consumers such as
    \c QoreLlmUtils::LlmTelemetry::normalizeUsage() and cost calculations must
    add them to the output tokens, while \c total_tokens already includes them.

    The cached input tokens (\c cachedContentTokenCount) are part of the prompt tokens and are returned in
    \c cached_content_token_count, \c cache_read_input_tokens and <tt>prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens</tt>
    when reported, and as \c 0 when the request used cached content (\a cache_requested) but the response
    reports none, so a cache miss is explicit.

    @param usage the Gemini \c usageMetadata
    @param cache_requested @ref True if the request used cached content

    @return OpenAI-style usage counters
*/
public hash<auto> sub normalizeUsage(auto usage, *bool cache_requested) {
    int prompt_tokens = usage.promptTokenCount ?? 0;
    int completion_tokens = usage.candidatesTokenCount ?? 0;
    int reasoning_tokens = usage.thoughtsTokenCount ?? 0;
    int total_tokens = usage.totalTokenCount
        ?? (prompt_tokens + completion_tokens + reasoning_tokens);
    hash<auto!> rv = {
        "prompt_tokens": prompt_tokens,
        "completion_tokens": completion_tokens,
        "total_tokens": total_tokens,
        "input_tokens": prompt_tokens,
        "output_tokens": completion_tokens,
        # thinking tokens are reported separately from the output tokens
        "reasoning_in_output": False,
    };
    if (exists usage.cachedContentTokenCount || cache_requested) {
        int cached_tokens = usage.cachedContentTokenCount ?? 0;
        rv.cached_content_token_count = cached_tokens;
        rv.cache_read_input_tokens = cached_tokens;
        rv.prompt_tokens_details = {"cached_tokens": cached_tokens};
    }
    if (reasoning_tokens > 0) {
        rv.reasoning_tokens = reasoning_tokens;
    }
    return rv;
}

#! Maps Gemini \c finishReason values to QoreLlmUtils stop reasons
public string sub mapFinishReason(*string reason) {
    switch (reason) {
        case "STOP":
            return "end_turn";
        case "MAX_TOKENS":
            return "max_tokens";
        case "SAFETY":
        case "RECITATION":
            return "content_filter";
        default:
            return reason ?? "end_turn";
    }
}

#! Maps Gemini \c finishReason values to OpenAI \c finish_reason values
public string sub finishReasonToOpenAi(*string reason) {
    switch (reason) {
        case "STOP":
            return "stop";
        case "MAX_TOKENS":
            return "length";
        case "SAFETY":
        case "RECITATION":
            return "content_filter";
        default:
            return reason ?? "stop";
    }
}

#! Translates an OpenAI \c tool_choice value to a Gemini \c toolConfig
public *hash<auto> sub openAiToolChoiceToGeminiConfig(auto choice) {
    if (!exists choice) {
        return NOTHING;
    }
    hash<auto!> cfg;
    if (choice == "none") {
        cfg.functionCallingConfig = {"mode": "NONE"};
    } else if (choice == "required") {
        cfg.functionCallingConfig = {"mode": "ANY"};
    } else if (choice == "auto") {
        cfg.functionCallingConfig = {"mode": "AUTO"};
    } else if (choice.typeCode() == NT_HASH && choice.function.name.val()) {
        cfg.functionCallingConfig = {
            "mode": "ANY",
            "allowedFunctionNames": (choice.function.name,),
        };
    }
    return cfg ? cfg : NOTHING;
}

#! Returns a failure detail string including the upstream provider error and status
/** On a non-2xx response the underlying REST exception carries the response body
    (with the provider's \c {error: {code, message, status}} payload) in \c ex.arg;
    this surfaces that message instead of just the bare HTTP status, so the cause
    of a rejection is visible.

    @param ex the REST exception caught from a request
    @return \c ex.desc, augmented with the upstream status and message when available
*/
public string sub requestErrorDetail(hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
    if (ex.arg.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
        return ex.desc;
    }
    auto body = ex.arg.body;
    if (body.typeCode() == NT_BINARY) {
        body = body.toString("UTF-8");
    }
    # an error body that was not deserialized, for example one sent with the Content-Type of an event stream,
    # is parsed here so the provider's message can be reported
    if (body.typeCode() == NT_STRING && body =~ /^\s*[\[{]/) {
        try {
            body = parse_json(body);
        } catch () {
        }
    }
    # streaming endpoints can wrap the error object in a list
    if (body.typeCode() == NT_LIST && body.size() == 1) {
        body = body[0];
    }
    *string msg;
    switch (body.typeCode()) {
        case NT_HASH:
            msg = body.error.message ?? body.error.status ?? body.message;
            break;
        case NT_STRING:
            msg = body;
            break;
    }
    if (!msg.val()) {
        return ex.desc;
    }
    return sprintf("%s (HTTP %s: %s)", ex.desc, ex.arg.status_code ?? "?", trim(msg));
}

#! Common provider base for Gemini-family models served over different transports
/** Holds everything shared between Gemini-on-AI-Studio (\c GeminiRestClient) and
    Gemini-on-Vertex (\c VertexAiRestClient): @ref chat(), @ref complete(),
    SSE streaming with @ref chatStream(), request-body building, and the
    OpenAI-compatible adapter hooks (\c tool_choice → \c toolConfig,
    \c response_format → output schema, body-option merging, and streaming
    tool-call harvesting).  Subclasses supply only transport and authentication
    via @ref createRestClient(), @ref getRequestPath(), @ref getRequestHeaders(),
    @ref getDefaultModel(), and (optionally) @ref getProviderLabel() and
    @ref getStreamRequestPath().

    Because the OpenAI/Gemini wire handling lives here once, the two providers
    cannot drift on tool/option/response behavior.

    @since GeminiBodyShape 1.0
*/
public class AbstractGeminiModelProvider inherits QoreLlmUtils::AbstractLlmProvider {
    private {
        #! Lazy-initialized REST client (a RestClientIo or subclass)
        *RestClientIo::RestClientIo rest_client;
        #! Serializes lazy initialization
        Mutex rest_mutex();
    }

    #! Creates the provider base from an @ref QoreLlmUtils::LlmBackendConfig
    constructor(hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmBackendConfig> config)
            : QoreLlmUtils::AbstractLlmProvider(config) {
    }

    #! Returns the provider's default model when none is supplied per request
    abstract string getDefaultModel();

    #! Builds the configured REST client for this provider's transport
    abstract RestClientIo::RestClientIo createRestClient();

    #! Returns the generateContent REST path for the given request
    abstract string getRequestPath(*hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts);

    #! Returns per-request auth headers (default: none — e.g. an API key in the client)
    *hash<auto> getRequestHeaders(*hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        return NOTHING;
    }

    #! Human-readable provider label used in error messages (default: the mode)
    string getProviderLabel() {
        return getMode();
    }

    #! Resolves the model for this request, falling back to @ref getDefaultModel()
    string getModelName(*hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        return getRequestModel(opts) ?? getDefaultModel();
    }

    hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmCompletionResult> complete(string system_prompt,
            string user_prompt, *hash<auto> output_schema,
            *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        hash<auto> body = buildModelRequest((
            <QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>{"role": "system", "content": system_prompt},
            <QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>{"role": "user", "content": user_prompt},
        ), NOTHING, output_schema, opts).body;
        hash<auto> resp = postGenerate(body, opts);
        return <QoreLlmUtils::LlmCompletionResult>{
            "content": GeminiBodyShape::extractText(resp.body),
            "usage": GeminiBodyShape::normalizeUsage(resp.body.usageMetadata, exists body.cachedContent),
        };
    }

    hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse> chat(
            list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>> messages,
            *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition>> tools,
            *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        hash<GeminiChatRequest> request = buildModelRequest(messages, tools, opts.output_schema, opts);
        hash<auto> resp = postGenerate(request.body, opts);
        hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatResponse> rv = GeminiBodyShape::parseChatResponse(resp.body,
            exists request.body.cachedContent, request.stringified_arguments);
        rv.model = getModelName(opts);
        return rv;
    }

    #! Streams a chat completion from the \c streamGenerateContent SSE endpoint
    /** Sends the request to @ref getStreamRequestPath() with the headers from
        @ref getRequestHeaders() and delivers each Gemini response chunk as
        exactly one @ref QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent, with the parsed chunk in
        \c raw and its text, if any, in \c delta.  The chunk with a
        \c finishReason, or with a \c promptFeedback.blockReason when the prompt
        was blocked, is delivered with \c done set and ends the stream; if the
        server closes the stream without one, a final \c done event without
        \c raw is delivered.

        @param messages conversation history
        @param callback receives each event as it arrives
        @param tools optional tool definitions
        @param opts per-call overrides; an explicit timeout bounds stream setup
            and all events together; otherwise the configured timeout limits each wait

        @throw LLM-ERROR the request failed or was rejected, the response was
        not an event stream, an event could not be parsed, the stream reported
        an error, or no event arrived within the request timeout
        @throw LLM-CANCELLED the request was cancelled with
        @ref QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions::cancellation "LlmRequestOptions::cancellation"; the connection
        of a stream in flight is closed at once
    */
    chatStream(list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>> messages,
            code<nothing(hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent>)> callback,
            *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition>> tools,
            *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        ensureRestClient();
        hash<GeminiChatRequest> request = buildModelRequest(messages, tools, opts.output_schema, opts);
        string path = getStreamRequestPath(opts);
        hash<auto> hdr = (getRequestHeaders(opts) ?? {}) + {
            "Content-Type": "application/json",
        };
        string json_body = make_json(request.body);
        *date request_deadline = exists opts.timeout_ms
            ? now_us() + milliseconds(getRequestTimeoutMs(opts)) : NOTHING;
        # a cancellation closes the connection of the request at once, also while its response is awaited
        list<int> cancel_ids = ();
        on_exit map removeRequestCancelHandler(opts, $1), cancel_ids;
        *code<nothing(HttpClientIo::HttpClientStreamHandle)> on_stream = opts.cancellation
            ? sub (HttpClientIo::HttpClientStreamHandle stream) {
                cancel_ids += addRequestCancelHandler(opts, sub () { stream.cancel(); });
            }
            : NOTHING;
        HttpClientStreamingIo::SseStreamReader reader;
        try {
            reader = withRetry(HttpClientStreamingIo::SseStreamReader sub () {
                return rest_client.restSseReaderWithTimeout("POST", path, hdr, json_body,
                    remainingStreamTimeout(getRequestTimeoutMs(opts), request_deadline), on_stream);
            }, opts);
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            if (ex.err == "LLM-CANCELLED") {
                rethrow;
            }
            throw "LLM-ERROR",
                sprintf("%s streaming request to %y failed: %s", getProviderLabel(), path,
                    GeminiBodyShape::requestErrorDetail(ex)), ex;
        }
        # a stream left before its end must not keep the server sending
        on_exit reader.cancel();
        deliverStreamEvents(reader, callback, getRequestTimeoutMs(opts), request_deadline, opts,
            request.stringified_arguments);
    }

    #! Explicit call deadlines cover the whole stream, not a fresh wait per chunk
    private static int remainingStreamTimeout(int timeout_ms, *date deadline) {
        if (!deadline) { return timeout_ms; }
        int remaining = (deadline - now_us()).durationMilliseconds();
        if (remaining <= 0) {
            throw "LLM-ERROR", "streaming request deadline exhausted",
                {"err": "HTTPCLIENT-TIMEOUT"};
        }
        return min(timeout_ms, remaining);
    }

    #! Returns the \c streamGenerateContent SSE path for the given request
    /** The default derives the path from @ref getRequestPath() by replacing its
        \c :generateContent method with \c :streamGenerateContent and requesting
        SSE framing with \c alt=sse.

        @param opts per-call overrides

        @return the streaming request path

        @throw LLM-CONFIG-ERROR the path returned by @ref getRequestPath() does
        not end with \c :generateContent
    */
    string getStreamRequestPath(*hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        string path = getRequestPath(opts);
        if (path !~ /:generateContent$/) {
            throw "LLM-CONFIG-ERROR",
                sprintf("%s request path %y does not end with \":generateContent\"; "
                    "cannot derive the streaming request path", getProviderLabel(), path);
        }
        path =~ s/:generateContent$/:streamGenerateContent/;
        return path + "?alt=sse";
    }

    #! Delivers the events of a Gemini SSE response stream to the callback
    /** @param reader the SSE reader of the response stream
        @param callback receives each event
        @param timeout_ms the maximum time to wait for each event
        @param deadline optional absolute deadline shared by all event waits
        @param opts optional per-call request overrides; a cancellation of
        @ref QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions::cancellation "LlmRequestOptions::cancellation" ends the delivery
        @param stringified_arguments the paths of the arguments that each tool of the request declares as JSON
        strings; the function calls of each chunk are delivered in \c raw with these arguments decoded
        (@ref GeminiBodyShape::decodeResponseToolArguments())

        @throw LLM-ERROR an event could not be parsed, the stream reported an
        error, or no event arrived within \a timeout_ms
        @throw LLM-CANCELLED the request was cancelled
    */
    private deliverStreamEvents(HttpClientStreamingIo::SseStreamReader reader,
            code<nothing(hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent>)> callback, int timeout_ms,
            *date deadline, *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts,
            *hash<string, list<list<*string>>> stringified_arguments) {
        while (True) {
            *hash<SseMessageInfo> evt = callCancellable(*hash<SseMessageInfo> sub () {
                return reader.readEvent(remainingStreamTimeout(timeout_ms, deadline));
            }, opts);
            if (!evt) {
                # the reader also returns nothing when the wait times out, which must not be reported as a
                # complete response
                if (!reader.isDone()) {
                    throw "LLM-ERROR",
                        sprintf("%s streaming response timed out: no event arrived within %d ms",
                            getProviderLabel(), timeout_ms), {"err": "HTTPCLIENT-TIMEOUT"};
                }
                callback(<QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent>{"done": True});
                return;
            }
            if (!evt.data.val()) {
                continue;
            }
            if (evt.data == "[DONE]") {
                callback(<QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent>{"done": True});
                return;
            }
            auto parsed;
            try {
                parsed = parse_json(evt.data);
            } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
                throw "LLM-ERROR",
                    sprintf("%s streaming response contained an event that is not valid JSON: %s",
                        getProviderLabel(), ex.desc), ex;
            }
            if (parsed.typeCode() != NT_HASH) {
                throw "LLM-ERROR",
                    sprintf("%s streaming response contained an event that is not a JSON object: %y",
                        getProviderLabel(), parsed);
            }
            # the chunk carries the function calls: their arguments are delivered with their declared types
            hash<auto> chunk = GeminiBodyShape::decodeResponseToolArguments(cast<hash>(parsed),
                stringified_arguments);
            if (chunk.error) {
                auto error = chunk.error;
                *string msg;
                *string code;
                if (error.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
                    msg = error.message ?? error.status;
                    if (exists error.code) {
                        code = error.code.toString();
                    }
                } else {
                    msg = error.toString();
                }
                throw "LLM-ERROR",
                    sprintf("%s streaming response reported an error: %s (code %s)", getProviderLabel(),
                        msg ?? "no message", code ?? "?"), error;
            }
            bool done = chunk.candidates[0].finishReason.val()
                || chunk.promptFeedback.blockReason.val();
            hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent> event = <QoreLlmUtils::ChatStreamEvent>{
                "done": done,
                "raw": chunk,
            };
            if (evt.event.val()) {
                event.event = evt.event;
            }
            string delta = GeminiBodyShape::extractText(chunk);
            if (delta.val()) {
                event.delta = delta;
            }
            callback(event);
            if (done) {
                return;
            }
        }
    }

    #! Merges \c body_options with Gemini nested \c generationConfig semantics
    hash<auto> mergeRequestBodyOptions(hash<auto> body,
            *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        if (!opts.body_options) {
            return body;
        }
        hash<auto!> rv;
        rv += body;
        # Canonicalize aliases before merging, so a snake_case override does not collide with the generated
        # camelCase configuration. Normalize again after merging to cover all effective request settings.
        hash<auto> extra = GeminiBodyShape::normalizeGenerationConfig(getModelName(opts), opts.body_options);
        foreach string key in (keys extra) {
            if (key == "generationConfig"
                    && rv.generationConfig.typeCode() == NT_HASH
                    && extra{key}.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
                hash<auto!> gc;
                gc += rv.generationConfig;
                gc += extra{key};
                rv.generationConfig = gc;
            } else {
                rv{key} = extra{key};
            }
        }
        return rv;
    }

    #! Translates an OpenAI \c tool_choice into Gemini's \c toolConfig form
    applyOpenAiToolChoice(reference<hash<auto!>> body_options, auto choice) {
        *hash<auto> tool_cfg = GeminiBodyShape::openAiToolChoiceToGeminiConfig(choice);
        if (tool_cfg) {
            body_options.toolConfig = tool_cfg;
        }
    }

    #! Routes an OpenAI \c response_format=json_schema to the request output schema
    applyOpenAiResponseFormat(reference<hash<auto!>> body_options,
            reference<hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions>> options,
            hash<auto> output_schema, *hash<auto> response_format) {
        options.output_schema = output_schema;
    }

    #! Updates OpenAI stream state from a Gemini-native event
    updateOpenAiStreamStateFromRaw(reference<hash<auto>> state, *hash<auto> raw) {
        if (!raw) {
            return;
        }
        hash<auto> cand = raw.candidates[0] ?? {};
        hash<auto> event_diagnostics =
            GeminiBodyShape::providerDiagnostics(raw, cand) ?? {};
        hash<auto!> diagnostics;
        if (state.provider_diagnostics.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            diagnostics += cast<hash>(state.provider_diagnostics);
        }
        diagnostics.wire_protocol = "gemini_generate_content";
        diagnostics.wire_stream_event_count =
            (diagnostics.wire_stream_event_count ?? 0).toInt() + 1;
        foreach string key in (("wire_candidate_count", "wire_part_count",
                "wire_text_part_count", "wire_function_call_count",
                "wire_other_part_count")) {
            int observed = (event_diagnostics{key} ?? 0).toInt();
            string max_key = key + "_max";
            if (observed > (diagnostics{max_key} ?? 0).toInt()) {
                diagnostics{max_key} = observed;
            }
        }
        if ((event_diagnostics.wire_text_observed ?? False).toBool()) {
            diagnostics.wire_text_observed = True;
        }
        if ((event_diagnostics.wire_function_call_observed ?? False).toBool()) {
            diagnostics.wire_function_call_observed = True;
        }
        # Retain only provider-owned protocol metadata; generated text and
        # tool arguments are never copied into diagnostics.
        foreach string key in (("response_id", "prompt_feedback",
                "usage_metadata", "finish_reason", "finish_message",
                "safety_ratings")) {
            if (exists event_diagnostics{key}) {
                diagnostics{key} = event_diagnostics{key};
            }
        }
        state.provider_diagnostics = diagnostics;
        if (raw.responseId.val()) {
            state.id = raw.responseId;
        } else if (raw.id.val()) {
            state.id = raw.id;
        }
        if (raw.model.val()) {
            state.model = raw.model;
        }
        if (raw.usageMetadata.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            state.usage = GeminiBodyShape::normalizeUsage(raw.usageMetadata);
        } else if (raw.usage.typeCode() == NT_HASH) {
            state.usage = raw.usage;
        }
        *string finish_reason = raw.candidates[0].finishReason;
        if (finish_reason.val()) {
            state.finish_reason = state.tool_calls
                ? "tool_calls" : GeminiBodyShape::finishReasonToOpenAi(finish_reason);
        } else if (raw.promptFeedback.blockReason.val()) {
            # the prompt was blocked, so no candidate was generated
            state.finish_reason = "content_filter";
        } else if (raw.choices[0].finish_reason.val()) {
            state.finish_reason = raw.choices[0].finish_reason;
        }
    }

    #! Harvests OpenAI-shaped \c tool_calls deltas from Gemini \c functionCall parts
    list<hash<auto>> getOpenAiToolCallDeltas(reference<hash<auto>> state,
            *hash<auto> raw) {
        if (!raw) {
            return ();
        }
        list<hash<auto>> streamed = ();
        foreach hash<auto> part in (raw.candidates[0].content.parts ?? ()) {
            if (!part.functionCall) {
                continue;
            }
            int idx = state.tool_calls.size();
            hash<auto!> tc = {
                "id": part.functionCall.id ?? sprintf("tool-%d", idx + 1),
                "type": "function",
                "function": {
                    "name": part.functionCall.name,
                    "arguments": make_json(part.functionCall.args ?? {}),
                },
            };
            # the reasoning signature is a sibling of `functionCall` on the part (see
            # parseChatResponse()); Gemini 3.x rejects a replayed call without it, so the streamed
            # harvest must carry it exactly like the non-streaming parse or every streamed tool
            # call poisons the conversation for the next request
            if (part.thoughtSignature.typeCode() == NT_STRING) {
                tc.thought_signature = part.thoughtSignature;
            }
            state.tool_calls += tc;
            streamed += {
                "index": idx,
                "id": tc.id,
                "type": "function",
                "function": tc.function,
            } + (tc.thought_signature.val()
                ? {"thought_signature": tc.thought_signature}
                : {});
        }
        return streamed;
    }

    #! Builds a generateContent request, honoring per-call knobs and body_options
    /** @return the request body and the paths of the arguments that each tool declares as JSON strings
    */
    private hash<GeminiChatRequest> buildModelRequest(
            list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ChatMessage>> messages,
            *list<hash<QoreLlmUtils::ToolDefinition>> tools,
            *hash<auto> output_schema,
            *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        *string cached_content = getRequestCachedContent(opts);
        hash<auto> resolved = {
            "model": getModelName(opts),
            "max_output_tokens": getRequestMaxOutputTokens(opts),
            "temperature": getRequestTemperature(opts),
            "reasoning_token_budget": getRequestReasoningTokenBudget(opts),
            "reasoning_effort": getRequestReasoningEffort(opts),
            "cached_content": cached_content,
        };
        hash<GeminiChatRequest> request = GeminiBodyShape::shapeChatRequest(messages, tools,
            output_schema, resolved);
        hash<auto> body = mergeRequestBodyOptions(request.body, opts);
        body = GeminiBodyShape::normalizeGenerationConfig(getModelName(opts), body);
        # body options such as a toolConfig translated from an OpenAI tool_choice must not be sent with a cache
        request.body = cached_content
            ? GeminiBodyShape::applyCachedContent(body, cached_content)
            : body;
        return request;
    }

    #! Returns the cached content resource that a request uses, if any
    /** @return @ref QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions::cached_content "LlmRequestOptions::cached_content", or a
        \c cachedContent given in \c body_options, resolved with @ref resolveCachedContentName()
    */
    *string getRequestCachedContent(*hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        *string name = opts.cached_content ?? opts.body_options.cachedContent;
        return name.val() ? resolveCachedContentName(name) : NOTHING;
    }

    #! Returns the full resource name for a cached content name or ID
    /** The base class returns names that have a \c / unchanged and prefixes IDs with \c "cachedContents/", the
        Gemini API form; providers with another resource layout override it

        @param name a cached content resource name or ID
    */
    string resolveCachedContentName(string name) {
        return name =~ /\// ? name : "cachedContents/" + name;
    }

    #! Posts a generateContent request through the provider transport and returns the response
    private hash<auto> postGenerate(hash<auto> body,
            *hash<QoreLlmUtils::LlmRequestOptions> opts) {
        ensureRestClient();
        string path = getRequestPath(opts);
        *hash<auto> hdr = getRequestHeaders(opts);
        try {
            return withRetry(hash<auto> sub () {
                return rest_client.restPostWithTimeout(path, body, hdr,
                    getRequestTimeoutMs(opts));
            }, opts);
        } catch (hash<ExceptionInfo> ex) {
            if (ex.err == "LLM-CANCELLED") {
                rethrow;
            }
            throw "LLM-ERROR",
                sprintf("%s request to %y failed: %s", getProviderLabel(), path,
                    GeminiBodyShape::requestErrorDetail(ex)), ex;
        }
    }

    #! Returns the lazily-initialized REST client (for subclass streaming overrides)
    private *RestClientIo::RestClientIo getRestClient() {
        return rest_client;
    }

    #! Lazy-initializes the REST client via @ref createRestClient()
    private ensureRestClient() {
        if (!rest_client) {
            rest_mutex.lock();
            on_exit rest_mutex.unlock();
            if (!rest_client) {
                rest_client = createRestClient();
            }
        }
    }
}
}
